    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0109" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg99"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 819.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of the 22d
                    ultimo, No. 561, which relates to the alleged enlistments on the Kearsarge. It
                    is not easy to discover the <pb facs="0110" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/> points of
                    difference between the consul’s statements and the opposing ones to which Earl
                    Russell refers. I can, therefore, only renew the instruction authorizing you to
                    investigate the matter, and remove the consul, if he has offended, reporting the
                    whole case to me.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
